# faces/charter.t88 - Charter 12, the first proportional face (SPEC.md 6.4)
#
# A 12-row proportional typeface for os8088, drawn to the grid SPEC.md 6.3's
# library sets type on. What it takes from the Macintosh is the PROPORTIONS
# rather than any outline - the same decision fonts/tallx.f8 records for the
# 8x8 cell, one size up and with the widths freed:
#
#   row 0   ascender top      b d f h k l
#   row 1   cap top           every capital and every digit
#   row 3   x-height top      every lowercase without an ascender
#   row 8   BASELINE ROW      the last ink row of anything that does not descend
#   rows 9-11                 g j p q y
#
# So capitals are 8 rows and the x-height is 6 - a ratio of 0.75, which is what
# makes a line of mostly-lowercase text read as a Macintosh at a glance, and
# which no fixed 8x8 cell has room to express.
#
# ADVANCES ARE 4, 6 OR 8 AND ALWAYS EVEN (SPEC.md 6.4). Even is not a
# typographic choice, it is what halves the library's pre-shifted table: a pen
# that starts on an even bit and advances evenly can only ever land on four of
# the eight bit phases (SPEC.md 6.5.2). At this size it costs the fitting very
# little, and a 2-pixel stem on a 2.4:1 CGA pixel wants even widths anyway.
#
# STEMS ARE 2 PIXELS in every letter and digit, for SPEC.md 6.2's measured
# reason: on a CGA at 640x200 the pixels are 2.4:1 tall, so a 1-pixel vertical
# stroke reads far thinner than a 1-pixel horizontal one and the face goes
# spindly on the adapter it is most likely to be read on. The symbols that are
# conventionally thin - # + = | / \ ~ ^ < > * - are drawn 1px and should be;
# tools/os88face.py's stem warning is letterforms only for that reason.
#
# Two shapes part company with the original on purpose, and both are a file
# manager's problem rather than a typographer's: capital I keeps its serifs,
# because a bare stem is pixel-identical to lowercase l in the middle of a file
# name, and every digit is drawn to the same 5-column width so that no figure
# is the odd one out in a column of numbers.

face Charter
rows 12
ascent 9
leading 2
aspect 0

style regular
psname Charter

